{%- comment -%}
  KK FWS Offer — PHASES 1, 2a and 2b (steps 1-3 + order summary).

  Built, and matched to the real Figma nodes (desktop `7420:1104` heading, `7420:1106`
  gallery, `7423:1590` step 1 size cards, `7423:1612` step 2 plan cards,
  `7423:1666` step 3 pay cards, `7422:145` CTA + trust row; mobile `7511:207`, step 2 at
  `7511:259`, step 3 at `7511:313`): section shell, eyebrow/heading/subheading, step 1
  (tower size), step 2 (protection plan), step 3 (pay mode), the order summary and the gallery — 1:1 slides,
  square edge-flush arrows, a four-across thumbnail strip, and video media as click-to-play
  posters.

  STEP 2 IS THE PRODUCT'S `Filter Type` OPTION. "Family Protection" and "Family Protection
  Plus" are marketing names for the two Filter Type values; each `plan` block names the
  option value it maps to. Size and plan together resolve one variant — see the matrix
  below.

  STEP 3 IS THE SELLING PLAN. "Subscribe & Save" posts the selected variant's Appstle
  selling plan; "One-Time Purchase" posts none. Appstle now carries one plan group per
  variant (six groups, one "Monthly Subscription" plan each, six-month cadence), so the
  allocation price is the design's subscription price exactly — $99 on every Family
  Protection tower, $149 on every Family Protection Plus. Step 2's card price is therefore
  DERIVED — the allocation price while subscribing, the variant price while paying once —
  and the authored `price` / `compare_price` block settings are only the fallback for a
  product whose variants carry no allocation. (This supersedes the merchandising gap in
  KK-FWS-CONVENTIONS.md §12: the design's $99/$149 were subscription prices all along.)

  THE ORDER SUMMARY follows the Figma frames that agree with what Shopify actually charges.
  The designer drew fourteen summary variants and they do not agree with each other; the
  reconciliation, and which frames are stale, is documented at the summary's data block
  below. Tower value and shipping are authored settings — neither figure exists in the
  product data.

  Stubbed (do not build here): the product accordion (mobile `7511:363`, desktop
  `7423:203`+).

  This section owns the `#kk-fws-offer` anchor. Five CTAs across the campaign page
  (offer bar, hero, header "Build Your System", comparison CTA, cards CTA) point at it.
  Do not remove the id, and do not change the root `<section>` element to a `<div>` —
  the theme's slider initialiser (`src/js/sliders.js`) calls
  `el.closest("section, aside").querySelector(...)` with no null check, so a missing
  `<section>` ancestor throws and breaks every slider on the page.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign size_option_name = section.settings.size_option_name | default: 'Size'
  assign filter_option_name = section.settings.filter_option_name | default: 'Filter Type'
  assign stand_option_name = section.settings.stand_option_name | default: 'Stand'

  assign pinned_stand = section.settings.stand_option_value

  comment
    Locate each option by name so the section survives a different campaign product
    with the options in a different order.
  endcomment
  assign size_index = -1
  assign filter_index = -1
  assign stand_index = -1

  for option_name in product.options
    if option_name == size_option_name
      assign size_index = forloop.index0
    elsif option_name == filter_option_name
      assign filter_index = forloop.index0
    elsif option_name == stand_option_name
      assign stand_index = forloop.index0
    endif
  endfor

  if size_index == -1
    assign size_index = 0
  endif

  comment
    Distinct size values, in variant order. Derived from the variants rather than
    `options_with_values` so the values are always plain strings.
  endcomment
  assign size_seen = '~~'
  for variant in product.variants
    assign size_value = variant.options[size_index]
    assign size_token = size_value | append: '~~'
    unless size_seen contains size_token
      assign size_seen = size_seen | append: size_token
    endunless
  endfor
  assign size_list = size_seen | remove_first: '~~' | split: '~~'

  comment
    Protection plan values, in the author's block order — the design's two cards are the
    product's two Filter Type values under marketing names, so the block order IS the card
    order. Falls back to the option's own values (then to a single unnamed plan) so the
    section still resolves a variant on a product whose plans have not been authored yet.
  endcomment
  assign filter_seen = '~~'
  for block in section.blocks
    if block.type == 'plan' and block.settings.filter_value != blank
      assign filter_token = block.settings.filter_value | append: '~~'
      unless filter_seen contains filter_token
        assign filter_seen = filter_seen | append: filter_token
      endunless
    endif
  endfor

  if filter_seen == '~~' and filter_index >= 0
    for variant in product.variants
      assign filter_value = variant.options[filter_index]
      assign filter_token = filter_value | append: '~~'
      unless filter_seen contains filter_token
        assign filter_seen = filter_seen | append: filter_token
      endunless
    endfor
  endif

  if filter_seen == '~~'
    assign filter_seen = '~~*~~'
  endif

  assign filter_list = filter_seen | remove_first: '~~' | split: '~~'

  comment
    The (size x plan) variant matrix. Both pickers are user-facing now, so a variant is
    resolved from the pair rather than from size alone with the filter pinned. Stand — an
    option the campaign product does not even have — stays pinned; `stand_index == -1`
    makes that a no-op.

    Each row also carries the variant's Appstle selling plan and both price faces, because
    step 3 switches between them. The campaign product's plan groups are one-plan-per-
    variant ("Monthly Subscription", delivered every 6 months), so `.first` is not a guess —
    there is exactly one allocation per variant. A variant with no allocation yields '0',
    which step 3 reads as "this pair cannot be subscribed to".

    Encoded as
      size~~filter~~variant_id~~available~~selling_plan_id~~sub_price~~sub_compare~~once_price
      ~~once_compare~~sub_recurring~~sub_upgrade
    where `sub_price` is the JOINING price (what checkout charges) and `sub_recurring` is the
    renewal price — equal on a one-cycle plan.
    with '0' for an unresolvable id and '-' for a money value the product does not carry.
    '-' rather than '' because Liquid's `split` silently drops empty segments and would
    shift every field after the gap.
  endcomment
  assign matrix = ''
  for size_value in size_list
    for filter_value in filter_list
      assign row_id = '0'
      assign row_available = '0'
      assign row_plan_id = '0'
      assign row_sub_price = '-'
      assign row_sub_recurring = '-'
      assign row_sub_recurring_cents = '0'
      assign row_sub_upgrade = '-'
      assign row_sub_compare = '-'
      assign row_once_price = '-'
      assign row_once_compare = '-'

      for variant in product.variants
        assign is_match = true

        unless variant.options[size_index] == size_value
          assign is_match = false
        endunless

        if is_match and filter_index >= 0 and filter_value != '*'
          unless variant.options[filter_index] == filter_value
            assign is_match = false
          endunless
        endif

        if is_match and stand_index >= 0 and pinned_stand != blank
          unless variant.options[stand_index] == pinned_stand
            assign is_match = false
          endunless
        endif

        if is_match
          assign row_id = variant.id
          if variant.available
            assign row_available = '1'
          endif

          assign row_once_price = variant.price | money_without_trailing_zeros
          if variant.compare_at_price > variant.price
            assign row_once_compare = variant.compare_at_price | money_without_trailing_zeros
          endif

          assign allocation = variant.selling_plan_allocations | first
          if allocation != blank
            assign row_plan_id = allocation.selling_plan.id

            comment
              TWO-CYCLE PRICING. Appstle plans take an `appstleCycles` list, so a plan can
              charge one price on the joining order and another on every renewal — the
              mechanism behind "pay the size upgrade up front, then $99 forever".

              `allocation.price` is what Shopify charges AT CHECKOUT, so it is always the
              due-today figure. The RENEWAL price is the LAST entry of
              `allocation.price_adjustments`: Shopify caps that array at two entries, so
              `last` is the joining price on a one-cycle plan and the recurring price on a
              two-cycle one. That is the whole fallback — a plan with a single cycle yields
              recurring == joining, an upgrade of zero, and exactly the behaviour this
              section had before two-cycle pricing existed.
            endcomment
            assign allocation_first_cents = allocation.price
            assign allocation_recurring_cents = allocation.price
            if allocation.price_adjustments.size > 0
              assign last_adjustment = allocation.price_adjustments | last
              assign allocation_recurring_cents = last_adjustment.price
            endif

            assign row_sub_price = allocation_first_cents | money_without_trailing_zeros
            assign row_sub_recurring = allocation_recurring_cents | money_without_trailing_zeros
            assign row_sub_recurring_cents = allocation_recurring_cents

            comment
              The joining premium the summary breaks out as "Size Upgrade" on a subscription.
              Zero on a one-cycle plan, which hides the row.
            endcomment
            assign upgrade_cents = allocation_first_cents | minus: allocation_recurring_cents
            if upgrade_cents > 0
              assign row_sub_upgrade = upgrade_cents | money_without_trailing_zeros
            endif

            comment
              The struck-through price beside the subscription price is the ONE-TIME price
              of the same variant ($99 vs $129) — that is the saving the design is showing,
              not the variant's own compare-at. Compared against the RECURRING price, since
              that is the number the card displays.
            endcomment
            if variant.price > allocation_recurring_cents
              assign row_sub_compare = variant.price | money_without_trailing_zeros
            endif
          endif

          break
        endif
      endfor

      assign matrix = matrix | append: size_value | append: '~~' | append: filter_value | append: '~~' | append: row_id | append: '~~' | append: row_available | append: '~~' | append: row_plan_id | append: '~~' | append: row_sub_price | append: '~~' | append: row_sub_compare | append: '~~' | append: row_once_price | append: '~~' | append: row_once_compare | append: '~~' | append: row_sub_recurring | append: '~~' | append: row_sub_upgrade | append: '~~' | append: row_sub_recurring_cents | append: '||'
    endfor
  endfor
  assign matrix_rows = matrix | split: '||'

  comment
    A size is offered when at least one plan resolves for it; a plan is offered when at
    least one size does. Encoded as "value~~available".
  endcomment
  assign resolved = ''
  assign selectable_count = 0
  assign first_selectable = ''
  for size_value in size_list
    assign row_available = '0'
    for row in matrix_rows
      assign parts = row | split: '~~'
      if parts[0] == size_value and parts[2] != '0' and parts[3] == '1'
        assign row_available = '1'
        break
      endif
    endfor
    if row_available == '1'
      assign selectable_count = selectable_count | plus: 1
      if first_selectable == ''
        assign first_selectable = size_value
      endif
    endif
    assign resolved = resolved | append: size_value | append: '~~' | append: row_available | append: '||'
  endfor
  assign resolved_rows = resolved | split: '||'

  assign plan_resolved = ''
  assign first_plan = ''
  for filter_value in filter_list
    assign row_available = '0'
    for row in matrix_rows
      assign parts = row | split: '~~'
      if parts[1] == filter_value and parts[2] != '0' and parts[3] == '1'
        assign row_available = '1'
        break
      endif
    endfor
    if row_available == '1' and first_plan == ''
      assign first_plan = filter_value
    endif
    assign plan_resolved = plan_resolved | append: filter_value | append: '~~' | append: row_available | append: '||'
  endfor
  assign plan_rows = plan_resolved | split: '||'

  comment
    Figma `7423:1592` carries a designer annotation: "On page load, the below configuration
    should be selected by default: 1.5 Gallon Tower / Family Protection Plan / Subscribe &
    Save." The first size block and the first plan block are that default, so honouring
    block order honours the annotation without hardcoding the values here. A ?variant=
    in the URL still wins, so shared links keep working.
  endcomment
  assign preferred_size = ''
  assign preferred_plan = ''
  if product.selected_variant != blank
    assign preferred_size = product.selected_variant.options[size_index]
    if filter_index >= 0
      assign preferred_plan = product.selected_variant.options[filter_index]
    endif
  endif

  assign default_size = first_selectable
  if preferred_size != blank
    for row in resolved_rows
      assign parts = row | split: '~~'
      if parts[0] == preferred_size and parts[1] == '1'
        assign default_size = preferred_size
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif

  assign default_plan = first_plan
  if preferred_plan != blank
    for row in plan_rows
      assign parts = row | split: '~~'
      if parts[0] == preferred_plan and parts[1] == '1'
        assign default_plan = preferred_plan
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif

  comment
    The variant the form posts before any JS runs. Falls back to the first resolvable pair
    for the default size so the button is never dead.
  endcomment
  assign default_variant_id = '0'
  for row in matrix_rows
    assign parts = row | split: '~~'
    if parts[0] == default_size and parts[1] == default_plan and parts[2] != '0'
      assign default_variant_id = parts[2]
      break
    endif
  endfor
  if default_variant_id == '0'
    for row in matrix_rows
      assign parts = row | split: '~~'
      if parts[0] == default_size and parts[2] != '0' and parts[3] == '1'
        assign default_variant_id = parts[2]
        assign default_plan = parts[1]
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif

  comment
    STEP 3 — how the customer pays. "Subscribe & Save" posts the pair's selling plan;
    "One-Time Purchase" posts no `selling_plan` at all. There is no third state, so this is
    a mode rather than a list of plans, and the same Figma annotation that pins 1.5 Gallon /
    Family Protection pins Subscribe & Save as the default.

    Subscribing is only offerable when the default pair actually has an allocation, so a
    product with no plans yet falls back to one-time and the step still renders honestly.
  endcomment
  assign default_row_sub_price = '-'
  assign default_row_sub_compare = '-'
  assign default_row_once_price = '-'
  assign default_row_once_compare = '-'
  assign default_selling_plan_id = '0'
  for row in matrix_rows
    assign parts = row | split: '~~'
    if parts[2] == default_variant_id
      assign default_selling_plan_id = parts[4]
      assign default_row_sub_price = parts[5]
      assign default_row_sub_compare = parts[6]
      assign default_row_once_price = parts[7]
      assign default_row_once_compare = parts[8]
      break
    endif
  endfor

  assign subscription_offered = false
  for row in matrix_rows
    assign parts = row | split: '~~'
    if parts[4] != '0'
      assign subscription_offered = true
      break
    endif
  endfor

  assign default_pay = 'subscribe'
  if default_selling_plan_id == '0'
    assign default_pay = 'onetime'
  endif

  comment
    ORDER SUMMARY figures (desktop `7423:1692` / `7423:2426` / `7423:2692`, mobile
    `7511:336`).

    The Figma frames disagree with each other on the arithmetic, so this follows the set
    that matches what Shopify will actually charge:

      Subscribe — tower FREE, plan at the allocation price, shipping.
                  Due today = allocation price + shipping ($108.95 / $158.95).
      One-time  — plan at the CHEAPEST size's price, the size delta broken out as
                  "Size Upgrade", shipping. No tower row.
                  Due today = variant price + shipping ($138.95 … $318.95).

    The frames showing "due today = size upgrade + shipping" ($39.95 / $69.95) would defer
    the first subscription payment, which this product cannot do: every Appstle allocation
    reports `checkout_charge` = 100%, so Shopify charges the full $99/$149 at checkout. The
    two 1.5 Gallon one-time frames ($387.95 / $507.95) bill the tower and the plan as
    separate lines, which double-counts a single variant price. Both are stale explorations.

    Tower value and shipping are AUTHORED — neither exists in the product data. There is no
    separate tower SKU (one variant price covers tower + filters), and real shipping is
    calculated by Shopify at checkout, so the shipping line here is a stated promise, not a
    quote. Held in cents so the totals are integer maths, then formatted once.
  endcomment
  assign shipping_cents = section.settings.shipping_cents
  assign tower_value_cents = section.settings.tower_value_cents

  comment
    The one-time summary shows the plan at its BASE price with the size premium on its own line
    ("Family Protection $129" + "Size Upgrade + $30" for a 2.25 Gallon).

    The base is the SMALLEST TOWER's variant, not the cheapest one. The design's premium is
    "+$30 for a bigger tower", which is relative to the smallest size — not to whichever variant
    happens to be cheapest. Using the cheapest broke twice: it let an un-repriced size supply the
    base for an already-repriced plan (a 1.5 Gallon at $378 showed a $159 plan component, because
    the untouched 2.25 Gallon was still $159), and it would invert every premium if a larger
    tower ever went on sale below a smaller one.
  endcomment
  assign base_size_value = size_list[0]
  assign plan_base = ''
  for filter_value in filter_list
    assign base_cents = 0
    for variant in product.variants
      assign counts = true
      unless variant.options[size_index] == base_size_value
        assign counts = false
      endunless
      if counts and filter_index >= 0 and filter_value != '*'
        unless variant.options[filter_index] == filter_value
          assign counts = false
        endunless
      endif
      if counts and stand_index >= 0 and pinned_stand != blank
        unless variant.options[stand_index] == pinned_stand
          assign counts = false
        endunless
      endif
      if counts
        assign base_cents = variant.price
        break
      endif
    endfor
    assign plan_base = plan_base | append: filter_value | append: '~~' | append: base_cents | append: '||'
  endfor
  assign plan_base_rows = plan_base | split: '||'

  comment
    DOES THE ONE-TIME PRICE INCLUDE THE TOWER?

    Ruled by the user: a one-time purchase pays for the tower, a subscription does not. So the
    variant price is tower + filters + size premium, and the summary itemises all three.

    Decided PER PLAN, not for the product as a whole: the test is whether the cheapest variant
    for that plan is dearer than the tower. When it is, the tower is part of the price and gets
    its own priced row, and the plan component is the remainder. When it is not, charging a tower
    on top would exceed the variant price, so the tower stays subscribe-only and the plan
    component is the whole variant price.

    Per plan matters because the plans are repriced one at a time. A single product-wide flag let
    an already-repriced plan answer for one that had not been touched yet, and the untouched plan
    rendered a NEGATIVE component (`Family Protection $-90`). Observed live, not theoretical.

    Encoded as "filter~~once_plan_cents~~tower_charged", tower_charged being '1' or '0'.
  endcomment
  assign plan_once = ''
  for row in plan_base_rows
    assign parts = row | split: '~~'
    assign candidate_base = parts[1] | plus: 0
    assign candidate_plan = candidate_base
    assign candidate_charged = '0'
    if candidate_base > tower_value_cents
      assign candidate_plan = candidate_base | minus: tower_value_cents
      assign candidate_charged = '1'
    endif
    assign plan_once = plan_once | append: parts[0] | append: '~~' | append: candidate_plan | append: '~~' | append: candidate_charged | append: '~~' | append: candidate_base | append: '||'
  endfor
  assign plan_once_rows = plan_once | split: '||'

  comment
    Marketing name for each Filter Type value, so the summary's plan row reads "Family
    Protection" rather than the raw option value.
  endcomment
  assign plan_names = ''
  for block in section.blocks
    if block.type == 'plan' and block.settings.filter_value != blank
      assign plan_label = block.settings.label | default: block.settings.filter_value
      assign plan_names = plan_names | append: block.settings.filter_value | append: '~~' | append: plan_label | append: '||'
    endif
  endfor
  assign plan_name_rows = plan_names | split: '||'

  comment
    Gallery media. The campaign product's media are NOT associated per variant
    (only one image is attached to any variant, and it is the same image for all of
    them), so `variant.featured_media` cannot drive the gallery. Per-size media is
    therefore author-controlled: each "Size details" block may name the product media
    positions for that size. When no block names any, every size shares one media set
    and the sync is a no-op — which is the truth for the current product data.
  endcomment
  assign media_limit = section.settings.media_limit
  assign default_positions_raw = ''
  assign default_count = 0
  for media in product.media
    if media.media_type == 'image' or media.media_type == 'video' or media.media_type == 'external_video'
      if media_limit > 0 and default_count >= media_limit
        break
      endif
      assign default_positions_raw = default_positions_raw | append: media.position | append: ','
      assign default_count = default_count | plus: 1
    endif
  endfor
  assign default_positions = default_positions_raw | split: ','

  assign media_varies = false
  for block in section.blocks
    if block.type == 'size_details' and block.settings.media_positions != blank
      assign media_varies = true
      break
    endif
  endfor

  comment
    Flatten every (size, media position) pair the gallery will render into one list, so
    the slides and the thumbnail strip are generated from a single source of truth and
    cannot drift out of index alignment. Encoded as "size~~position".
  endcomment
  assign slide_pairs = ''
  for row in resolved_rows
    assign parts = row | split: '~~'
    assign size_value = parts[0]

    assign positions = default_positions

    if media_varies
      for block in section.blocks
        if block.type == 'size_details' and block.settings.size_value == size_value and block.settings.media_positions != blank
          assign positions = block.settings.media_positions | replace: ' ', '' | split: ','
          break
        endif
      endfor
    endif

    for position in positions
      assign media_index = position | plus: 0 | minus: 1
      assign media = product.media[media_index]
      if media != blank
        if media.media_type == 'image' or media.media_type == 'video' or media.media_type == 'external_video'
          assign slide_pairs = slide_pairs | append: size_value | append: '~~' | append: position | append: '||'
        endif
      endif
    endfor

    unless media_varies
      break
    endunless
  endfor
  assign slide_list = slide_pairs | split: '||'
-%}

<section
  id="kk-fws-offer"
  class="kk-fws-offer"
  data-kk-fws-pay-mode="{{ default_pay }}"
  style="
    --kk-fws-offer-background: {{ section.settings.background_color }};
    --kk-fws-offer-heading: {{ section.settings.heading_color }};
    --kk-fws-offer-text: {{ section.settings.text_color }};
    --kk-fws-offer-card-background: {{ section.settings.card_background_color }};
    --kk-fws-offer-card-border: {{ section.settings.card_border_color }};
    --kk-fws-offer-card-selected-background: {{ section.settings.card_selected_background_color }};
    --kk-fws-offer-card-selected-border: {{ section.settings.card_selected_border_color }};
    --kk-fws-offer-button-background: {{ section.settings.button_background_color }};
    --kk-fws-offer-button-text: {{ section.settings.button_text_color }};
    --kk-fws-offer-line: {{ section.settings.line_color }};
    --kk-fws-offer-eyebrow-background: {{ section.settings.eyebrow_background_color }};
    --kk-fws-offer-nav-background: {{ section.settings.nav_background_color }};
    --kk-fws-offer-thumb-border: {{ section.settings.thumb_border_color }};
    --kk-fws-offer-badge-background: {{ section.settings.badge_background_color }};
    --kk-fws-offer-badge-text: {{ section.settings.badge_text_color }};
    --kk-fws-offer-step-background: {{ section.settings.step_background_color }};
    --kk-fws-offer-step-text: {{ section.settings.step_text_color }};
    --kk-fws-offer-compare: {{ section.settings.compare_price_color }};
  "
>
  <div class="kk-fws-offer__container">
    {%- if section.settings.eyebrow != blank -%}
      <p class="kk-fws-offer__eyebrow">
        {{- section.settings.eyebrow | replace: '[month]', '<span class="dyn-month"></span>' -}}
      </p>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
      <h2 class="kk-fws-offer__heading">{{ section.settings.heading }}</h2>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if section.settings.subheading != blank -%}
      <p class="kk-fws-offer__subheading">
        {{- section.settings.subheading | replace: '[month]', '<span class="dyn-month"></span>' -}}
      </p>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if product == blank -%}
      <p class="kk-fws-offer__notice">
        This section needs a product. Preview it on a product template.
      </p>
    {%- else -%}
      <div class="kk-fws-offer__layout">
        <div class="kk-fws-offer__media">
          <div
            id="product-slider"
            class="swiper-container swiper kk-fws-offer__slider"
            data-slidestoshow="1"
            aria-label="{{ product.title | escape }} media gallery"
          >
            <div class="swiper-wrapper">
              {%- for pair in slide_list -%}
                {%- liquid
                  assign slide_parts = pair | split: '~~'
                  assign size_value = slide_parts[0]
                  assign media_index = slide_parts[1] | plus: 0 | minus: 1
                  assign media = product.media[media_index]
                  assign media_alt = media.alt | default: product.title
                -%}
                <div
                  class="swiper-slide kk-fws-offer__slide"
                  {% if media_varies %}data-kk-fws-size="{{ size_value | escape }}"{% endif %}
                >
                  {%- if media.media_type == 'image' -%}
                    {{
                      media.preview_image
                      | image_url: width: 1140
                      | image_tag:
                        class: 'kk-fws-offer__slide-image',
                        loading: 'lazy',
                        widths: '375, 570, 750, 1140',
                        sizes: '(max-width: 749px) calc(100vw - 4rem), 569px',
                        alt: media_alt
                    }}
                  {%- else -%}
                    {%- comment -%}
                      Video media render as their poster with a play affordance. The player is
                      only injected on click (see the gallery script) so a gallery of videos
                      does not load several players up front.
                    {%- endcomment -%}
                    <div
                      class="kk-fws-offer__video"
                      data-kk-fws-video
                      {% if media.media_type == 'external_video' %}
                        data-kk-fws-video-embed="{{ media | external_video_url: autoplay: 'true' | escape }}"
                      {% else %}
                        data-kk-fws-video-src="{{ media.sources.last.url | escape }}"
                      {% endif %}
                    >
                      {{
                        media.preview_image
                        | image_url: width: 1140
                        | image_tag:
                          class: 'kk-fws-offer__slide-image',
                          loading: 'lazy',
                          widths: '375, 570, 750, 1140',
                          sizes: '(max-width: 749px) calc(100vw - 4rem), 569px',
                          alt: media_alt
                      }}
                      <button class="kk-fws-offer__play" type="button">
                        <span class="sr-only">Play video</span>
                      </button>
                    </div>
                  {%- endif -%}
                </div>
              {%- else -%}
                <div class="swiper-slide kk-fws-offer__slide">
                  {{ 'product-1' | placeholder_svg_tag: 'kk-fws-offer__slide-image' }}
                </div>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </div>

            <button
              class="swiper-prev kk-fws-offer__nav kk-fws-offer__nav--prev"
              type="button"
              aria-label="Previous image"
            >
              <img
                class="kk-fws-offer__nav-icon"
                src="{{ 'kk-fws-icon-chevron.svg' | asset_url }}"
                alt=""
                width="12"
                height="21"
                aria-hidden="true"
              >
            </button>
            <button
              class="swiper-next kk-fws-offer__nav kk-fws-offer__nav--next"
              type="button"
              aria-label="Next image"
            >
              <img
                class="kk-fws-offer__nav-icon"
                src="{{ 'kk-fws-icon-chevron.svg' | asset_url }}"
                alt=""
                width="12"
                height="21"
                aria-hidden="true"
              >
            </button>
          </div>

          {%- comment -%}
            The thumbnail strip is a plain grid, NOT a `.control` Swiper. The theme's
            `.control` branch in src/js/sliders.js forces a 2-column, 2-row grid at >=768px
            (and `control-five` a 2x3), none of which is the design's single 4-across row.
            Driving `window.sliders['product-slider'].slideTo()` directly is both simpler
            and exact. The class must not be `control`, or initSlider would adopt it.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if slide_list.size > 1 -%}
            <div class="kk-fws-offer__thumbs" data-kk-fws-thumbs role="tablist" aria-label="Gallery thumbnails">
              {%- for pair in slide_list -%}
                {%- liquid
                  assign slide_parts = pair | split: '~~'
                  assign size_value = slide_parts[0]
                  assign media_index = slide_parts[1] | plus: 0 | minus: 1
                  assign media = product.media[media_index]
                -%}
                <button
                  class="kk-fws-offer__thumb"
                  type="button"
                  role="tab"
                  data-kk-fws-thumb="{{ forloop.index0 }}"
                  {% if media_varies %}data-kk-fws-size="{{ size_value | escape }}"{% endif %}
                  aria-label="Show image {{ forloop.index }}"
                  aria-selected="{% if forloop.first %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}"
                >
                  {{
                    media.preview_image
                    | image_url: width: 300
                    | image_tag:
                      class: 'kk-fws-offer__thumb-image',
                      loading: 'lazy',
                      widths: '150, 300',
                      sizes: '135px',
                      alt: ''
                  }}
                  {%- unless media.media_type == 'image' -%}
                    <span class="kk-fws-offer__thumb-play" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                  {%- endunless -%}
                </button>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>

        <div class="kk-fws-offer__panel">
          {%- if selectable_count == 0 -%}
            <p class="kk-fws-offer__notice">
              {{ section.settings.unavailable_text }}
            </p>
          {%- else -%}
            {%- form 'product', product, id: 'kk-fws-offer-form', class: 'kk-fws-offer__form', novalidate: 'novalidate' -%}
              {%- comment -%}
                The posted variant. Size and plan are two separate radio groups that
                together identify one variant, so neither can be `name="id"` on its own.
                Rendered with the default pair already resolved server-side, so the form
                adds the right variant even before the picker script runs.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              <input type="hidden" name="id" value="{{ default_variant_id }}" data-kk-fws-variant-id>

              {%- comment -%}
                STEP 3's posted value. A DISABLED input is not submitted at all, which is
                exactly the "One-Time Purchase" state — there is no selling_plan value that
                means "no subscription", so the field has to disappear from the payload
                rather than post an empty string (Shopify rejects `selling_plan=`).

                `data-kk-fws-selling-plan` also marks this input as OURS, so the Appstle
                guard below can neutralise the app's injected radios without touching it.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              <input
                type="hidden"
                name="selling_plan"
                value="{{ default_selling_plan_id }}"
                data-kk-fws-selling-plan
                {% if default_pay != 'subscribe' or default_selling_plan_id == '0' %}disabled{% endif %}
              >

              <fieldset class="kk-fws-offer__sizes">
                <legend class="kk-fws-offer__step">
                  <span class="kk-fws-offer__step-number" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
                  <span class="kk-fws-offer__step-title">{{ section.settings.size_legend }}</span>
                </legend>

                <div class="kk-fws-offer__size-list">
                  {%- for row in resolved_rows -%}
                    {%- liquid
                      assign parts = row | split: '~~'
                      assign size_value = parts[0]
                      assign is_available = false
                      if parts[1] == '1'
                        assign is_available = true
                      endif

                      assign size_label = size_value
                      assign size_description = ''
                      assign size_badge = ''

                      for block in section.blocks
                        if block.type == 'size_details' and block.settings.size_value == size_value
                          if block.settings.label != blank
                            assign size_label = block.settings.label
                          endif
                          assign size_description = block.settings.description
                          assign size_badge = block.settings.badge
                          break
                        endif
                      endfor
                    -%}

                    <label class="kk-fws-offer__size">
                      <input
                        class="kk-fws-offer__size-input"
                        type="radio"
                        name="kk-fws-size"
                        value="{{ size_value | escape }}"
                        data-kk-fws-size="{{ size_value | escape }}"
                        {% if size_value == default_size %}checked{% endif %}
                        {% unless is_available %}disabled{% endunless %}
                      >
                      <span class="kk-fws-offer__size-card">
                        <img
                          class="kk-fws-offer__size-tick"
                          src="{{ 'kk-fws-icon-size-selected.svg' | asset_url }}"
                          alt=""
                          width="23"
                          height="23"
                          aria-hidden="true"
                          loading="lazy"
                        >
                        <span class="kk-fws-offer__size-text">
                          <span class="kk-fws-offer__size-name">{{ size_label }}</span>
                          {%- if size_description != blank -%}
                            <span class="kk-fws-offer__size-description">{{ size_description }}</span>
                          {%- endif -%}
                        </span>
                        {%- if size_badge != blank -%}
                          <span class="kk-fws-offer__size-badge">{{ size_badge }}</span>
                        {%- endif -%}
                        {%- unless is_available -%}
                          <span class="kk-fws-offer__size-unavailable">
                            {{ section.settings.sold_out_text }}
                          </span>
                        {%- endunless -%}
                      </span>
                    </label>
                  {%- endfor -%}
                </div>
              </fieldset>

              {%- comment -%}
                STEP 2 — the protection plan, i.e. the product's Filter Type option under
                marketing names (Figma desktop `7423:1612`, mobile `7511:259`). Two cards
                side by side at every breakpoint; mobile narrows them rather than stacking.
                Prices are authored per block — see the note at the top of this file.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              {%- assign plan_blocks = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'plan' -%}
              {%- if plan_blocks.size > 0 -%}
                <fieldset class="kk-fws-offer__plans">
                  <legend class="kk-fws-offer__step">
                    <span class="kk-fws-offer__step-number" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
                    <span class="kk-fws-offer__step-title">{{ section.settings.plan_legend }}</span>
                  </legend>

                  <div class="kk-fws-offer__plan-list">
                    {%- for block in plan_blocks -%}
                      {%- liquid
                        assign filter_value = block.settings.filter_value
                        assign is_available = false
                        for row in plan_rows
                          assign parts = row | split: '~~'
                          if parts[0] == filter_value and parts[1] == '1'
                            assign is_available = true
                            break
                          endif
                        endfor

                        assign features = block.settings.features | newline_to_br | split: '<br />'

                        comment
                          Both price faces for this plan at the DEFAULT size, so the card is
                          already correct before the picker script runs. The subscription
                          price is size-invariant on this product ($99 / $149 for every
                          tower), which is why the design can show one number per plan; the
                          one-time price is not, so JS rewrites these on every change.
                          Authored `price` / `compare_price` remain the fallback for a
                          product whose variants carry no allocation.
                        endcomment
                        assign card_sub_price = '-'
                        assign card_sub_recurring = '-'
                        assign card_sub_recurring_cents = 0
                        assign card_sub_compare = '-'
                        assign card_once_price = '-'
                        assign card_once_compare = '-'
                        for matrix_row in matrix_rows
                          assign card_parts = matrix_row | split: '~~'
                          if card_parts[0] == default_size and card_parts[1] == filter_value
                            assign card_sub_price = card_parts[5]
                            assign card_sub_compare = card_parts[6]
                            assign card_once_price = card_parts[7]
                            assign card_once_compare = card_parts[8]
                            assign card_sub_recurring = card_parts[9]
                            assign card_sub_recurring_cents = card_parts[11] | plus: 0
                            break
                          endif
                        endfor

                        comment
                          Step 2 is about the PLAN, so both faces use the plan component rather
                          than the whole system price: the renewal price while subscribing, the
                          plan's one-time price while paying once, and the latter struck through
                          on the subscribe face. That is exactly what Figma prints ($99 / $129).
                        endcomment
                        assign card_once_plan = '-'
                        assign card_once_plan_cents = 0
                        comment
                          Step 2 prints ONE number per plan, so it uses the plan price at the
                          base size — the canonical figure, independent of which size is selected.
                        endcomment
                        for base_row in plan_once_rows
                          assign base_parts = base_row | split: '~~'
                          if base_parts[0] == filter_value
                            assign card_once_plan_cents = base_parts[1] | plus: 0
                            assign card_once_plan = card_once_plan_cents | money_without_trailing_zeros
                            break
                          endif
                        endfor

                        if default_pay == 'subscribe' and card_sub_recurring != '-'
                          assign card_price = card_sub_recurring
                          assign card_cadence = block.settings.price_note
                          comment
                            Strike the one-time plan price only when it is genuinely higher than
                            the renewal price. A strikethrough BELOW the price reads as a price
                            rise, and a misconfigured tower value can produce exactly that.
                          endcomment
                          assign card_compare = ''
                          if card_once_plan_cents > card_sub_recurring_cents
                            assign card_compare = card_once_plan
                          endif
                        elsif card_once_plan != '-'
                          assign card_price = card_once_plan
                          assign card_cadence = ''
                          assign card_compare = ''
                        else
                          assign card_price = block.settings.price
                          assign card_cadence = block.settings.price_note
                          assign card_compare = block.settings.compare_price
                        endif

                        if card_compare == '-'
                          assign card_compare = ''
                        endif
                      -%}

                      <label class="kk-fws-offer__plan" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                        <input
                          class="kk-fws-offer__plan-input"
                          type="radio"
                          name="kk-fws-plan"
                          value="{{ filter_value | escape }}"
                          data-kk-fws-plan="{{ filter_value | escape }}"
                          {% if filter_value == default_plan %}checked{% endif %}
                          {% unless is_available %}disabled{% endunless %}
                        >
                        <span class="kk-fws-offer__plan-card">
                          {%- if block.settings.ribbon != blank -%}
                            <span class="kk-fws-offer__plan-ribbon">{{ block.settings.ribbon }}</span>
                          {%- endif -%}

                          <span class="kk-fws-offer__plan-body">
                            <span class="kk-fws-offer__plan-name">
                              <span class="kk-fws-offer__plan-radio" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                              <span class="kk-fws-offer__plan-label">{{ block.settings.label | default: filter_value }}</span>
                            </span>

                            {%- if card_price != blank -%}
                              {%- comment -%}
                                The three price nodes are always present (hidden, not
                                removed, when empty) so step 3 can rewrite them without
                                having to build DOM.
                              {%- endcomment -%}
                              <span
                                class="kk-fws-offer__plan-price"
                                data-kk-fws-plan-price
                                data-cadence="{{ block.settings.price_note | escape }}"
                                data-once-plan="{{ card_once_plan | escape }}"
                              >
                                <span class="kk-fws-offer__plan-amount" data-kk-fws-plan-amount>
                                  {{- card_price -}}
                                </span>
                                <span
                                  class="kk-fws-offer__plan-cadence"
                                  data-kk-fws-plan-cadence
                                  {% if card_cadence == blank %}hidden{% endif %}
                                >
                                  {{- card_cadence -}}
                                </span>
                                <s
                                  class="kk-fws-offer__plan-compare"
                                  data-kk-fws-plan-compare
                                  {% if card_compare == blank %}hidden{% endif %}
                                >
                                  {{- card_compare -}}
                                </s>
                              </span>
                            {%- endif -%}

                            {%- if features.size > 0 -%}
                              <span class="kk-fws-offer__plan-features">
                                {%- for feature in features -%}
                                  {%- assign feature_text = feature | strip_newlines | strip -%}
                                  {%- if feature_text != blank -%}
                                    <span class="kk-fws-offer__plan-feature">
                                      <img
                                        class="kk-fws-offer__plan-check"
                                        src="{{ 'kk-fws-icon-check.svg' | asset_url }}"
                                        alt=""
                                        width="13"
                                        height="9"
                                        aria-hidden="true"
                                        loading="lazy"
                                      >
                                      <span class="kk-fws-offer__plan-feature-text">{{ feature_text }}</span>
                                    </span>
                                  {%- endif -%}
                                {%- endfor -%}
                              </span>
                            {%- endif -%}

                            {%- unless is_available -%}
                              <span class="kk-fws-offer__plan-unavailable">
                                {{ section.settings.sold_out_text }}
                              </span>
                            {%- endunless -%}
                          </span>
                        </span>
                      </label>
                    {%- endfor -%}
                  </div>
                </fieldset>
              {%- endif -%}

              {%- comment -%}
                STEP 3 — how would you like to pay? (Figma desktop `7423:1666`, mobile
                `7511:313`.) Two cards, same visual language as step 2 but shorter: ribbon,
                radio, name, one line of copy, no price and no feature list.

                Rendered only when the product actually has selling plans. With none, there
                is no choice to offer — every purchase is one-time — and showing a dead
                toggle would be worse than showing nothing.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              {%- if subscription_offered -%}
                <fieldset class="kk-fws-offer__pays">
                  <legend class="kk-fws-offer__step">
                    <span class="kk-fws-offer__step-number" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
                    <span class="kk-fws-offer__step-title">{{ section.settings.pay_legend }}</span>
                  </legend>

                  <div class="kk-fws-offer__pay-list">
                    <label class="kk-fws-offer__pay">
                      <input
                        class="kk-fws-offer__pay-input"
                        type="radio"
                        name="kk-fws-pay"
                        value="subscribe"
                        data-kk-fws-pay="subscribe"
                        {% if default_pay == 'subscribe' %}checked{% endif %}
                      >
                      <span class="kk-fws-offer__pay-card">
                        {%- if section.settings.subscribe_ribbon != blank -%}
                          <span class="kk-fws-offer__pay-ribbon">{{ section.settings.subscribe_ribbon }}</span>
                        {%- endif -%}

                        <span class="kk-fws-offer__pay-body">
                          <span class="kk-fws-offer__pay-name">
                            <span class="kk-fws-offer__pay-radio" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                            <span class="kk-fws-offer__pay-label">{{ section.settings.subscribe_label }}</span>
                          </span>

                          {%- if section.settings.subscribe_description != blank -%}
                            <span class="kk-fws-offer__pay-description">
                              {{- section.settings.subscribe_description -}}
                            </span>
                          {%- endif -%}

                          {%- comment -%}
                            Only reachable when the selected size/plan pair has no allocation
                            while some other pair does — the card stays visible and greys out
                            rather than vanishing, matching how step 2 handles the same case.
                          {%- endcomment -%}
                          <span class="kk-fws-offer__pay-unavailable">
                            {{ section.settings.pay_unavailable_text }}
                          </span>
                        </span>
                      </span>
                    </label>

                    <label class="kk-fws-offer__pay">
                      <input
                        class="kk-fws-offer__pay-input"
                        type="radio"
                        name="kk-fws-pay"
                        value="onetime"
                        data-kk-fws-pay="onetime"
                        {% if default_pay != 'subscribe' %}checked{% endif %}
                      >
                      <span class="kk-fws-offer__pay-card">
                        {%- if section.settings.onetime_ribbon != blank -%}
                          <span class="kk-fws-offer__pay-ribbon">{{ section.settings.onetime_ribbon }}</span>
                        {%- endif -%}

                        <span class="kk-fws-offer__pay-body">
                          <span class="kk-fws-offer__pay-name">
                            <span class="kk-fws-offer__pay-radio" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                            <span class="kk-fws-offer__pay-label">{{ section.settings.onetime_label }}</span>
                          </span>

                          {%- if section.settings.onetime_description != blank -%}
                            <span class="kk-fws-offer__pay-description">
                              {{- section.settings.onetime_description -}}
                            </span>
                          {%- endif -%}
                        </span>
                      </span>
                    </label>
                  </div>
                </fieldset>
              {%- endif -%}

              {%- comment -%}
                ORDER SUMMARY — desktop `7423:1692`, mobile `7511:336`. Every figure is
                rendered server-side for the default configuration and rewritten by the
                picker script; nothing here is a static number.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              {%- if section.settings.show_summary -%}
                {%- liquid
                  assign summary_variant = nil
                  for variant in product.variants
                    comment
                      `default_variant_id` came out of the matrix as a string, and Liquid's
                      `if` cannot take a filter, so the cast needs its own assign.
                    endcomment
                    assign variant_id_string = variant.id | append: ''
                    if variant_id_string == default_variant_id
                      assign summary_variant = variant
                      break
                    endif
                  endfor

                  assign summary_plan_label = default_plan
                  for row in plan_name_rows
                    assign parts = row | split: '~~'
                    if parts[0] == default_plan
                      assign summary_plan_label = parts[1]
                      break
                    endif
                  endfor

                  assign summary_base_cents = summary_variant.price
                  for row in plan_base_rows
                    assign parts = row | split: '~~'
                    if parts[0] == default_plan
                      assign summary_base_cents = parts[1] | plus: 0
                      break
                    endif
                  endfor

                  assign summary_upgrade_cents = summary_variant.price | minus: summary_base_cents
                  assign summary_subscribing = false
                  if default_pay == 'subscribe' and default_selling_plan_id != '0'
                    assign summary_subscribing = true
                  endif

                  if summary_subscribing
                    assign summary_allocation = summary_variant.selling_plan_allocations | first
                    assign summary_first_cents = summary_allocation.price
                    assign summary_recurring_cents = summary_allocation.price
                    if summary_allocation.price_adjustments.size > 0
                      assign summary_last_adjustment = summary_allocation.price_adjustments | last
                      assign summary_recurring_cents = summary_last_adjustment.price
                    endif

                    assign summary_plan_amount = summary_recurring_cents | money_without_trailing_zeros
                    assign summary_total_cents = summary_first_cents | plus: shipping_cents
                    assign summary_upgrade_cents = summary_first_cents | minus: summary_recurring_cents
                    assign summary_note = section.settings.subscribe_note | replace: '[price]', summary_plan_amount
                    assign summary_footnote = section.settings.subscribe_footnote | replace: '[value]', section.settings.tower_value_cents | money_without_trailing_zeros
                  else
                    comment
                      Same split as the per-variant data below — see the note there.
                    endcomment
                    if summary_upgrade_cents < 0
                      assign summary_upgrade_cents = 0
                    endif
                    assign summary_once_plan_cents = summary_variant.price | minus: summary_upgrade_cents
                    assign summary_tower_charged = false
                    if summary_once_plan_cents > tower_value_cents
                      assign summary_once_plan_cents = summary_once_plan_cents | minus: tower_value_cents
                      assign summary_tower_charged = true
                    endif
                    assign summary_plan_amount = summary_once_plan_cents | money_without_trailing_zeros
                    assign summary_total_cents = summary_variant.price | plus: shipping_cents
                    assign summary_note = section.settings.onetime_note
                    assign summary_footnote = section.settings.onetime_footnote
                  endif

                  comment
                    The tower row is priced on a one-time purchase and FREE on a subscription.
                    It is hidden entirely only when a one-time purchase does not carry the tower
                    (the pre-reprice fallback) AND the customer is paying once.
                  endcomment
                  assign show_tower_row = true
                  unless summary_subscribing
                    unless summary_tower_charged
                      assign show_tower_row = false
                    endunless
                  endunless
                -%}

                <div class="kk-fws-offer__summary" data-kk-fws-summary>
                  <p class="kk-fws-offer__summary-title">{{ section.settings.summary_legend }}</p>

                  <div class="kk-fws-offer__summary-rows">
                    {%- comment -%}
                      Tower row — subscription only. On a one-time purchase the tower is not
                      free, and the variant price already covers it, so the row would be
                      double-counting (the mistake the two stale 1.5 Gallon frames make).
                    {%- endcomment -%}
                    <div
                      class="kk-fws-offer__summary-row"
                      data-kk-fws-summary-row="tower"
                      {% unless show_tower_row %}hidden{% endunless %}
                    >
                      <span class="kk-fws-offer__summary-label">
                        {{ section.settings.tower_label }} -
                        <span data-kk-fws-summary-size>{{ default_size }}</span>
                      </span>
                      <span class="kk-fws-offer__summary-value">
                        {%- comment -%}
                          Subscribing strikes the tower value and reads FREE; paying once shows
                          the same figure as a real charge. One row, two faces.
                        {%- endcomment -%}
                        <s
                          class="kk-fws-offer__summary-strike"
                          data-kk-fws-summary-tower-strike
                          {% unless summary_subscribing %}hidden{% endunless %}
                        >
                          {{- tower_value_cents | money_without_trailing_zeros -}}
                        </s>
                        <span class="kk-fws-offer__summary-amount" data-kk-fws-summary-tower-amount>
                          {%- if summary_subscribing -%}
                            {{- section.settings.tower_free_text -}}
                          {%- else -%}
                            {{- tower_value_cents | money_without_trailing_zeros -}}
                          {%- endif -%}
                        </span>
                      </span>
                    </div>

                    {%- comment -%}
                      Size upgrade, directly under the tower it applies to (Figma `7423:2426`).
                      On a ONE-TIME purchase this is the variant price above the base size. On a SUBSCRIPTION it is the joining premium — the gap
                      between what checkout charges and what renewals cost. Either way the row
                      appears only when there is something to charge, so a one-cycle plan
                      (where joining == recurring) hides it exactly as before.
                    {%- endcomment -%}
                    <div
                      class="kk-fws-offer__summary-row"
                      data-kk-fws-summary-row="upgrade"
                      {% if summary_upgrade_cents <= 0 %}hidden{% endif %}
                    >
                      <span class="kk-fws-offer__summary-label">
                        {{- section.settings.size_upgrade_label -}}
                      </span>
                      <span class="kk-fws-offer__summary-value">
                        <span class="kk-fws-offer__summary-amount" data-kk-fws-summary-upgrade>
                          + {{ summary_upgrade_cents | money_without_trailing_zeros }}
                        </span>
                      </span>
                    </div>

                    <div class="kk-fws-offer__summary-row" data-kk-fws-summary-row="plan">
                      <span class="kk-fws-offer__summary-label" data-kk-fws-summary-plan-label>
                        {{- summary_plan_label -}}
                      </span>
                      <span class="kk-fws-offer__summary-value">
                        <span class="kk-fws-offer__summary-amount" data-kk-fws-summary-plan-amount>
                          {{- summary_plan_amount -}}
                        </span>
                        <span
                          class="kk-fws-offer__summary-cadence"
                          data-kk-fws-summary-plan-cadence
                          {% unless summary_subscribing %}hidden{% endunless %}
                        >
                          {{- section.settings.summary_cadence -}}
                        </span>
                      </span>
                    </div>

                    <div class="kk-fws-offer__summary-row" data-kk-fws-summary-row="shipping">
                      <span class="kk-fws-offer__summary-label">
                        {{- section.settings.shipping_label -}}
                      </span>
                      <span class="kk-fws-offer__summary-value">
                        <span class="kk-fws-offer__summary-amount">
                          {{- shipping_cents | money_without_trailing_zeros -}}
                        </span>
                      </span>
                    </div>
                  </div>

                  <div class="kk-fws-offer__summary-due">
                    <div class="kk-fws-offer__summary-due-text">
                      <p class="kk-fws-offer__summary-due-label">
                        {{- section.settings.due_today_label -}}
                      </p>
                      <p class="kk-fws-offer__summary-note" data-kk-fws-summary-note>
                        {{- summary_note -}}
                      </p>
                    </div>
                    <p class="kk-fws-offer__summary-total" data-kk-fws-summary-total>
                      {{- summary_total_cents | money_without_trailing_zeros -}}
                    </p>
                  </div>

                  <p class="kk-fws-offer__summary-footnote">
                    <img
                      class="kk-fws-offer__summary-footnote-icon"
                      src="{{ 'kk-fws-icon-check-circle.svg' | asset_url }}"
                      alt=""
                      width="14"
                      height="14"
                      aria-hidden="true"
                      loading="lazy"
                    >
                    <span data-kk-fws-summary-footnote>{{ summary_footnote }}</span>
                  </p>
                </div>
              {%- endif -%}

              <button class="kk-fws-offer__button" type="submit" name="add">
                {{- section.settings.button_label -}}
              </button>

              {%- assign trust_blocks = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'trust' -%}
              {%- if trust_blocks.size > 0 -%}
                <ul class="kk-fws-offer__trust-list">
                  {%- for block in trust_blocks -%}
                    <li class="kk-fws-offer__trust" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                      {%- render 'kk-fws-offer-icon', block: block -%}
                      <span class="kk-fws-offer__trust-text">{{ block.settings.text }}</span>
                    </li>
                  {%- endfor -%}
                </ul>
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endform -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</section>

{%- comment -%}
  Appstle guard. The app injects its own `selling_plan` radios into every product form on the
  page and pre-checks one of them. Left alone, the form posts whichever plan the app decided
  on instead of the one step 3 resolved. Confirmed in the browser, not theoretical.

  Now that step 3 exists this no longer means "never subscribe" — it means the ONLY control
  allowed to set `selling_plan` is this section's own hidden input. Appstle's radios are
  disabled (never submitted) rather than removed, so the app's own scripts still find their
  nodes. Re-runs on mutation because the app injects asynchronously and can re-inject.

  This block is deliberately OUTSIDE the `media_varies` conditional below — it must run on
  every render, not only when the gallery sync happens to be emitted.
{%- endcomment -%}
<script>
  (function () {
    var root = document.getElementById('kk-fws-offer');
    var form = root && root.querySelector('form[action*="/cart/add"]');

    if (!form) {
      return;
    }

    function neutraliseSellingPlan() {
      // `:not([data-kk-fws-selling-plan])` is the whole point of this selector now: step 3
      // owns a real selling_plan input, and this guard must not switch it off.
      var planInputs = form.querySelectorAll('[name="selling_plan"]:not([data-kk-fws-selling-plan])');

      for (var i = 0; i < planInputs.length; i++) {
        planInputs[i].checked = false;
        planInputs[i].disabled = true;
      }
    }

    neutraliseSellingPlan();
    document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', neutraliseSellingPlan);
    window.addEventListener('load', neutraliseSellingPlan);

    if (window.MutationObserver) {
      new MutationObserver(neutraliseSellingPlan).observe(form, {
        childList: true,
        subtree: true,
      });
    }
  })();
</script>

{%- comment -%}
  Size x plan -> variant, and (size x plan x pay mode) -> selling plan and price.

  The three pickers are separate radio groups (none can be `name="id"` alone), so this keeps
  the form's hidden `id` and hidden `selling_plan` in step with them, greys out any plan that
  has no variant for the selected size, and rewrites step 2's prices when the pay mode
  changes. The server already rendered the default triple, so with JS off the form still
  adds a real, correctly priced variant on the default subscription.
{%- endcomment -%}
<script type="application/json" data-kk-fws-variants>
  [
    {%- for row in matrix_rows -%}
      {%- assign parts = row | split: '~~' -%}
      {
        "size": {{ parts[0] | json }},
        "plan": {{ parts[1] | json }},
        "id": {{ parts[2] | json }},
        "available": {% if parts[3] == '1' %}true{% else %}false{% endif %},
        "sellingPlan": {{ parts[4] | json }},
        "subPrice": {{ parts[5] | json }},
        "subCompare": {{ parts[6] | json }},
        "oncePrice": {{ parts[7] | json }},
        "onceCompare": {{ parts[8] | json }},
        "subRecurring": {{ parts[9] | json }},
        "subUpgrade": {{ parts[10] | json }},
        "subRecurringCents": {{ parts[11] | plus: 0 }}
      }{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
    {%- endfor -%}
  ]
</script>

{%- comment -%}
  ORDER SUMMARY figures per variant. Keyed by variant id so the picker script can look them
  up straight from the matrix row it already resolved, rather than re-deriving prices in JS
  where the money format would have to be reimplemented.
{%- endcomment -%}
<script type="application/json" data-kk-fws-summary-data>
  {
    {%- assign summary_first = true -%}
    {%- for variant in product.variants -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign include_variant = true
        if stand_index >= 0 and pinned_stand != blank
          unless variant.options[stand_index] == pinned_stand
            assign include_variant = false
          endunless
        endif
      -%}
      {%- if include_variant -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign v_filter = ''
          if filter_index >= 0
            assign v_filter = variant.options[filter_index]
          endif

          assign v_plan_label = v_filter
          for row in plan_name_rows
            assign parts = row | split: '~~'
            if parts[0] == v_filter
              assign v_plan_label = parts[1]
              break
            endif
          endfor

          assign v_base_cents = variant.price
          for row in plan_base_rows
            assign parts = row | split: '~~'
            if parts[0] == v_filter
              assign v_base_cents = parts[1] | plus: 0
              break
            endif
          endfor

          assign v_once_total = variant.price | plus: shipping_cents

          comment
            SPLIT THE ONE-TIME PRICE: tower + plan + size premium, derived so the three ALWAYS
            add back up to the variant price. That invariant is what keeps the summary's rows
            summing to due-today in every state, including a half-finished reprice.

              premium = variant price - base size's price, floored at zero
              plan    = variant price - premium          (i.e. the base size's price)
              tower   = charged only when the plan still clears the tower value, and then
                        deducted from the plan

            Flooring the premium matters while a reprice is in flight: an un-repriced size can
            cost LESS than the repriced base, which would otherwise yield a negative premium and
            a plan component that no longer reconciles. Deducting the tower only when the plan
            exceeds it is what keeps the component positive without a separate clamp.
          endcomment
          assign v_upgrade_cents = variant.price | minus: v_base_cents
          if v_upgrade_cents < 0
            assign v_upgrade_cents = 0
          endif

          assign v_once_plan_cents = variant.price | minus: v_upgrade_cents
          assign v_tower_charged = false
          if v_once_plan_cents > tower_value_cents
            assign v_once_plan_cents = v_once_plan_cents | minus: tower_value_cents
            assign v_tower_charged = true
          endif

          comment
            Subscribe side. `price` is the joining charge (due today); the last price
            adjustment is the renewal. See the two-cycle note in the matrix above.
          endcomment
          assign v_allocation = variant.selling_plan_allocations | first
          assign v_sub_amount = ''
          assign v_sub_upgrade = ''
          assign v_sub_total = ''
          if v_allocation != blank
            assign v_first_cents = v_allocation.price
            assign v_recurring_cents = v_allocation.price
            if v_allocation.price_adjustments.size > 0
              assign v_last_adjustment = v_allocation.price_adjustments | last
              assign v_recurring_cents = v_last_adjustment.price
            endif

            comment
              The plan row shows the RENEWAL price, which is the number the design puts on
              the card ($99 / 6 months). The joining premium goes on its own Size Upgrade
              row so the rows still sum to due today.
            endcomment
            assign v_sub_amount = v_recurring_cents | money_without_trailing_zeros
            assign v_sub_total = v_first_cents | plus: shipping_cents | money_without_trailing_zeros

            assign v_sub_upgrade_cents = v_first_cents | minus: v_recurring_cents
            if v_sub_upgrade_cents > 0
              assign v_sub_upgrade = v_sub_upgrade_cents | money_without_trailing_zeros
            endif
          endif

          assign v_tower_value = tower_value_cents | money_without_trailing_zeros
          assign v_sub_note = section.settings.subscribe_note | replace: '[price]', v_sub_amount
          assign v_sub_footnote = section.settings.subscribe_footnote | replace: '[value]', v_tower_value
        -%}
        {%- unless summary_first %},{% endunless -%}
        {%- assign summary_first = false -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          `append: ''` before `json` so the key is a quoted string — `variant.id | json` on a
          number emits a bare numeric key, which is not valid JSON.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {{ variant.id | append: '' | json }}: {
          "size": {{ variant.options[size_index] | json }},
          "planLabel": {{ v_plan_label | json }},
          "base": {{ v_once_plan_cents | money_without_trailing_zeros | json }},
          "towerCharged": {{ v_tower_charged | json }},
          "towerValue": {{ tower_value_cents | money_without_trailing_zeros | json }},
          "upgrade": {% if v_upgrade_cents > 0 %}{{ v_upgrade_cents | money_without_trailing_zeros | json }}{% else %}""{% endif %},
          "subAmount": {{ v_sub_amount | json }},
          "subUpgrade": {{ v_sub_upgrade | json }},
          "subTotal": {{ v_sub_total | json }},
          "onceTotal": {{ v_once_total | money_without_trailing_zeros | json }},
          "subNote": {{ v_sub_note | json }},
          "onceNote": {{ section.settings.onetime_note | json }},
          "subFootnote": {{ v_sub_footnote | json }},
          "onceFootnote": {{ section.settings.onetime_footnote | json }}
        }
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  }
</script>

<script>
  (function () {
    var root = document.getElementById('kk-fws-offer');

    if (!root) {
      return;
    }

    // The matrix script block is a sibling of the section, not a descendant of it — like every
    // other script in this file it is emitted after the closing section tag.
    var data = document.querySelector('[data-kk-fws-variants]');
    var target = root.querySelector('[data-kk-fws-variant-id]');
    var button = root.querySelector('.kk-fws-offer__button');

    if (!data || !target) {
      return;
    }

    var rows;

    try {
      rows = JSON.parse(data.textContent);
    } catch (error) {
      return;
    }

    var sizeInputs = [].slice.call(root.querySelectorAll('.kk-fws-offer__size-input'));
    var planInputs = [].slice.call(root.querySelectorAll('.kk-fws-offer__plan-input'));
    var payInputs = [].slice.call(root.querySelectorAll('.kk-fws-offer__pay-input'));
    var sellingPlanTarget = root.querySelector('[data-kk-fws-selling-plan]');

    var summaryCard = root.querySelector('[data-kk-fws-summary]');
    var summaryData = document.querySelector('[data-kk-fws-summary-data]');
    var summary = null;

    // The authored "FREE" label, read off whatever Liquid rendered so the string stays in the
    // schema rather than being duplicated here. Only meaningful when the server rendered the
    // subscribe face, hence the letters test and the hard default.
    var towerFreeText = 'FREE';
    var towerAmountNode = summaryCard && summaryCard.querySelector('[data-kk-fws-summary-tower-amount]');

    if (towerAmountNode && /[a-z]/i.test(towerAmountNode.textContent)) {
      towerFreeText = towerAmountNode.textContent.trim();
    }

    if (summaryCard && summaryData) {
      try {
        summary = JSON.parse(summaryData.textContent);
      } catch (error) {
        summary = null;
      }
    }

    function checkedValue(inputs) {
      for (var i = 0; i < inputs.length; i++) {
        if (inputs[i].checked) {
          return inputs[i].value;
        }
      }
      return null;
    }

    function find(size, plan) {
      for (var i = 0; i < rows.length; i++) {
        if (rows[i].size === size && rows[i].plan === plan) {
          return rows[i];
        }
      }
      return null;
    }

    // '-' is the Liquid side's "this product has no such price", not a value to render.
    function money(value) {
      return value && value !== '-' ? value : '';
    }

    // Step 2's price is the SELECTED pay mode's price. Subscribing shows the allocation
    // price with the cadence and the one-time price struck through; paying once shows the
    // variant price with no cadence. A plan whose pair has no allocation keeps whatever
    // the server rendered rather than being blanked.
    function paintPlanPrice(input, size, pay) {
      var card = input.nextElementSibling;
      var wrap = card && card.querySelector('[data-kk-fws-plan-price]');

      if (!wrap) {
        return;
      }

      var row = find(size, input.value);

      if (!row) {
        return;
      }

      var subscribing = pay === 'subscribe' && row.sellingPlan !== '0';

      // Step 2 is about the PLAN, so both faces use the plan component: the renewal price
      // while subscribing, the plan's one-time price while paying once. That one-time plan
      // price is constant per plan, so it rides on the wrapper as a data attribute rather
      // than being looked up per variant.
      var oncePlan = wrap.getAttribute('data-once-plan') || '';
      oncePlan = oncePlan === '-' ? '' : oncePlan;

      var amount = subscribing
        ? money(row.subRecurring) || money(row.subPrice)
        : oncePlan || money(row.oncePrice);

      if (!amount) {
        return;
      }

      var cadence = subscribing ? wrap.getAttribute('data-cadence') || '' : '';
      // Struck through on the subscribe face only: plan-vs-plan, the saving the design shows.
      // Suppressed when it is not actually a saving — a strikethrough below the price reads as
      // a price rise, which a misconfigured tower value can produce.
      var compare = '';

      if (subscribing) {
        var oncePlanCents = oncePlan ? Math.round(parseFloat(oncePlan.replace(/[^0-9.]/g, '')) * 100) : 0;

        if (oncePlanCents > (row.subRecurringCents || 0)) {
          compare = oncePlan;
        } else if (!oncePlan) {
          compare = money(row.subCompare);
        }
      }

      var amountNode = wrap.querySelector('[data-kk-fws-plan-amount]');
      var cadenceNode = wrap.querySelector('[data-kk-fws-plan-cadence]');
      var compareNode = wrap.querySelector('[data-kk-fws-plan-compare]');

      if (amountNode) {
        amountNode.textContent = amount;
      }

      if (cadenceNode) {
        cadenceNode.textContent = cadence;
        cadenceNode.hidden = !cadence;
      }

      if (compareNode) {
        compareNode.textContent = compare;
        compareNode.hidden = !compare;
      }
    }

    // Order summary. Mirrors the Liquid that rendered the default state, so the server and
    // the client can never disagree about the arithmetic — both read the same per-variant
    // figures out of [data-kk-fws-summary-data].
    function paintSummary(match, pay) {
      if (!summary || !match) {
        return;
      }

      var figures = summary[match.id];

      if (!figures) {
        return;
      }

      var subscribing = pay === 'subscribe' && match.sellingPlan !== '0' && !!figures.subTotal;

      function row(name) {
        return summaryCard.querySelector('[data-kk-fws-summary-row="' + name + '"]');
      }

      function text(hook, value) {
        var node = summaryCard.querySelector('[data-kk-fws-summary-' + hook + ']');

        if (node) {
          node.textContent = value;
        }
      }

      var towerRow = row('tower');
      var upgradeRow = row('upgrade');
      var cadence = summaryCard.querySelector('[data-kk-fws-summary-plan-cadence]');

      // Tower: FREE on a subscription, a real charge on a one-time purchase. Hidden only when
      // paying once on a product whose one-time price does not carry the tower.
      if (towerRow) {
        towerRow.hidden = !subscribing && !figures.towerCharged;

        var strike = summaryCard.querySelector('[data-kk-fws-summary-tower-strike]');

        if (strike) {
          strike.hidden = !subscribing;
        }

        text('tower-amount', subscribing ? towerFreeText : figures.towerValue);
      }

      // Size premium. One-time: the variant price above the cheapest size. Subscribe: the
      // joining premium, i.e. what checkout charges above the renewal price. Shown only when
      // there is something to charge — a one-cycle plan has no subscribe-side premium, which
      // keeps the row hidden on subscribe exactly as before two-cycle pricing.
      if (upgradeRow) {
        var upgrade = subscribing ? figures.subUpgrade : figures.upgrade;

        upgradeRow.hidden = !upgrade;

        if (upgrade) {
          text('upgrade', '+ ' + upgrade);
        }
      }

      if (cadence) {
        cadence.hidden = !subscribing;
      }

      text('size', figures.size);
      text('plan-label', figures.planLabel);
      text('plan-amount', subscribing ? figures.subAmount : figures.base);
      text('total', subscribing ? figures.subTotal : figures.onceTotal);
      text('note', subscribing ? figures.subNote : figures.onceNote);
      text('footnote', subscribing ? figures.subFootnote : figures.onceFootnote);
    }

    function sync() {
      var size = checkedValue(sizeInputs);
      var plan = planInputs.length ? checkedValue(planInputs) : null;

      // A plan with no variant for the selected size is disabled, not hidden — the card
      // is part of the offer's argument even when one size can't take it.
      for (var i = 0; i < planInputs.length; i++) {
        var row = find(size, planInputs[i].value);
        var usable = !!(row && row.id !== '0' && row.available);

        planInputs[i].disabled = !usable;
        planInputs[i].closest('.kk-fws-offer__plan').classList.toggle('is-unavailable', !usable);

        if (!usable && planInputs[i].checked) {
          planInputs[i].checked = false;
          plan = null;
        }
      }

      if (planInputs.length && !plan) {
        for (var j = 0; j < planInputs.length; j++) {
          if (!planInputs[j].disabled) {
            planInputs[j].checked = true;
            plan = planInputs[j].value;
            break;
          }
        }
      }

      var match = find(size, plan);
      var pay = payInputs.length ? checkedValue(payInputs) : 'onetime';

      // Step 3, same rule as step 2: a pair with no allocation cannot be subscribed to, so
      // "Subscribe & Save" greys out and the choice falls back to one-time.
      var subscribable = !!(match && match.sellingPlan && match.sellingPlan !== '0');

      for (var k = 0; k < payInputs.length; k++) {
        if (payInputs[k].value !== 'subscribe') {
          continue;
        }

        payInputs[k].disabled = !subscribable;
        payInputs[k].closest('.kk-fws-offer__pay').classList.toggle('is-unavailable', !subscribable);

        if (!subscribable && payInputs[k].checked) {
          payInputs[k].checked = false;
          pay = null;
        }
      }

      if (payInputs.length && !pay) {
        for (var m = 0; m < payInputs.length; m++) {
          if (!payInputs[m].disabled) {
            payInputs[m].checked = true;
            pay = payInputs[m].value;
            break;
          }
        }
      }

      for (var n = 0; n < planInputs.length; n++) {
        paintPlanPrice(planInputs[n], size, pay);
      }

      paintSummary(match, pay);

      // Step 1's badges are the ONE-TIME size deltas, and the user ruled they must not show on
      // a one-time purchase now that the tower is charged there. Reflected as state on the root
      // so the hiding is one CSS rule rather than per-node DOM work.
      root.setAttribute('data-kk-fws-pay-mode', pay === 'subscribe' ? 'subscribe' : 'onetime');

      // One-time is the ABSENCE of a selling_plan, so the input is disabled rather than
      // emptied — see the note on the input itself.
      if (sellingPlanTarget) {
        if (pay === 'subscribe' && subscribable) {
          sellingPlanTarget.value = match.sellingPlan;
          sellingPlanTarget.disabled = false;
        } else {
          sellingPlanTarget.disabled = true;
        }
      }

      if (match && match.id !== '0' && match.available) {
        target.value = match.id;
        target.disabled = false;

        if (button) {
          button.disabled = false;
        }

        return;
      }

      // Nothing resolves: disabling the input rather than posting a stale id means the
      // form cannot silently add the previously selected variant.
      target.disabled = true;

      if (button) {
        button.disabled = true;
      }
    }

    for (var i = 0; i < sizeInputs.length; i++) {
      sizeInputs[i].addEventListener('change', sync);
    }

    for (var j = 0; j < planInputs.length; j++) {
      planInputs[j].addEventListener('change', sync);
    }

    for (var k = 0; k < payInputs.length; k++) {
      payInputs[k].addEventListener('change', sync);
    }

    sync();
  })();
</script>

{%- comment -%}
  Gallery behaviour: thumbnail strip, video slides, and (when the author has given each
  size its own media positions) keeping the visible slides inside the selected size's group.

  Swiper is an ES module inside assets/main.js and is NOT a global, so this cannot construct
  or configure the instance. The theme's initialiser registers it at
  window.sliders['product-slider']; everything here drives that public instance.
{%- endcomment -%}
<script>
  (function () {
    var root = document.getElementById('kk-fws-offer');

    if (!root) {
      return;
    }

    var slider = root.querySelector('.kk-fws-offer__slider');

    if (!slider) {
      return;
    }

    var slides = [].slice.call(slider.querySelectorAll('.swiper-wrapper > .swiper-slide'));
    var thumbs = [].slice.call(root.querySelectorAll('[data-kk-fws-thumb]'));
    var groupsEnabled = {% if media_varies %}true{% else %}false{% endif %};

    var reduced =
      window.matchMedia && window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;

    // The theme initialises its sliders on DOM ready; this script runs inline, so the
    // instance may not exist yet. Poll briefly rather than racing it.
    function whenReady(callback) {
      var attempts = 0;

      (function poll() {
        var instance = window.sliders ? window.sliders[slider.id] : null;

        if (instance && typeof instance.slideTo === 'function') {
          callback(instance);
          return;
        }

        if (++attempts > 60) {
          return;
        }

        window.setTimeout(poll, 100);
      })();
    }

    function currentSize() {
      var checked = root.querySelector('.kk-fws-offer__size-input:checked');
      return checked ? checked.getAttribute('data-kk-fws-size') : null;
    }

    // Inclusive [first, last] slide indices belonging to the selected size. Without
    // grouping every slide is in range.
    function groupBounds() {
      if (!groupsEnabled) {
        return [0, slides.length - 1];
      }

      var size = currentSize();
      var first = -1;
      var last = -1;

      for (var i = 0; i < slides.length; i++) {
        if (slides[i].getAttribute('data-kk-fws-size') === size) {
          if (first < 0) {
            first = i;
          }
          last = i;
        }
      }

      return first < 0 ? [0, slides.length - 1] : [first, last];
    }

    function syncThumbs(activeIndex) {
      var bounds = groupBounds();

      for (var i = 0; i < thumbs.length; i++) {
        var index = parseInt(thumbs[i].getAttribute('data-kk-fws-thumb'), 10);
        var inGroup = index >= bounds[0] && index <= bounds[1];

        thumbs[i].hidden = !inGroup;
        thumbs[i].setAttribute('aria-selected', index === activeIndex ? 'true' : 'false');
        thumbs[i].classList.toggle('is-active', index === activeIndex);
      }
    }

    whenReady(function (instance) {
      syncThumbs(instance.activeIndex);

      for (var i = 0; i < thumbs.length; i++) {
        thumbs[i].addEventListener('click', function (event) {
          var index = parseInt(event.currentTarget.getAttribute('data-kk-fws-thumb'), 10);
          instance.slideTo(index, reduced ? 0 : 400);
        });
      }

      instance.on('slideChange', function () {
        // Slides for every size live in one wrapper (hiding them fights Swiper's layout),
        // so a swipe can run past the selected size's images into the next size's. Snap
        // back to the nearest in-group slide instead of letting the two sets bleed.
        var bounds = groupBounds();
        var index = instance.activeIndex;

        if (index < bounds[0]) {
          instance.slideTo(bounds[0], 0);
          return;
        }

        if (index > bounds[1]) {
          instance.slideTo(bounds[1], 0);
          return;
        }

        syncThumbs(index);
      });

      if (groupsEnabled) {
        var inputs = root.querySelectorAll('.kk-fws-offer__size-input');

        for (var j = 0; j < inputs.length; j++) {
          inputs[j].addEventListener('change', function (event) {
            if (!event.target.checked) {
              return;
            }

            instance.slideTo(groupBounds()[0], reduced ? 0 : 400);
            syncThumbs(groupBounds()[0]);
          });
        }
      }
    });

    // Video slides render as a poster; the player is only built when asked for.
    root.addEventListener('click', function (event) {
      var trigger = event.target.closest ? event.target.closest('.kk-fws-offer__play') : null;

      if (!trigger) {
        return;
      }

      var holder = trigger.closest('[data-kk-fws-video]');

      if (!holder || holder.querySelector('video, iframe')) {
        return;
      }

      var embed = holder.getAttribute('data-kk-fws-video-embed');
      var src = holder.getAttribute('data-kk-fws-video-src');
      var player;

      if (embed) {
        player = document.createElement('iframe');
        player.setAttribute('src', embed);
        player.setAttribute('allow', 'autoplay; encrypted-media; picture-in-picture');
        player.setAttribute('allowfullscreen', 'allowfullscreen');
        player.setAttribute('title', 'Product video');
      } else if (src) {
        player = document.createElement('video');
        player.setAttribute('src', src);
        player.setAttribute('controls', 'controls');
        player.setAttribute('playsinline', 'playsinline');
        player.setAttribute('autoplay', 'autoplay');
      } else {
        return;
      }

      player.className = 'kk-fws-offer__video-player';
      holder.appendChild(player);
      trigger.hidden = true;
    });
  })();
</script>

